  "title": "Journal becomes a run store: schema, chain, index, reader",
  "summary": "The single-file journal module is split into five: a versioned event model with a JSON Schema, a hash module that separates the chain hash from a new replay digest, a per-work-item run index guarded by a file lock, and a reader that validates every line and link before returning anything. The journal moves from `<state>/buffer` to `<state>/runs`, gains run-started/run-complete/attention/review/finding/state-change event types, and a new `osf run start|complete` CLI drives it. Checkpoint and review writers are updated to the new actor and grade types.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
